1
00:00:05,670 --> 00:00:09,740
(Hwang In Youp)

2
00:00:09,880 --> 00:00:14,720
(Lee Hye Ri)

3
00:00:16,480 --> 00:00:21,990
(Baek Sung Chul, Lee Yul Eum)

4
00:00:34,870 --> 00:00:39,069
(Dream To You)

5
00:00:39,070 --> 00:00:40,169
(All people, events, and backgrounds are fictional.)

6
00:00:40,170 --> 00:00:41,179
(This drama includes footage created using AI.)

7
00:00:41,180 --> 00:00:42,180
(Children and animals were filmed under strict safety guidelines.)

8
00:00:42,580 --> 00:00:44,550
(Episode 3)

9
00:00:51,350 --> 00:00:52,820
Excuse me.

10
00:01:12,070 --> 00:01:13,540
Hello, Director.

11
00:01:14,210 --> 00:01:15,480
You were here.

12
00:01:15,910 --> 00:01:17,180
You got here earlier than expected.

13
00:01:19,350 --> 00:01:20,550
Wait, I'll get you some clothes.

14
00:01:21,320 --> 00:01:22,320
No, it's okay...

15
00:01:53,950 --> 00:01:56,920
You actually looked better before. Less of a jerk.

16
00:01:57,480 --> 00:01:58,550
Go inside and change.

17
00:02:30,520 --> 00:02:31,720
So, why did you come looking for me?

18
00:02:32,320 --> 00:02:33,850
Aren't you curious how I found you?

19
00:02:35,060 --> 00:02:36,890
Someone's been following me for the past few days.

20
00:03:03,980 --> 00:03:07,820
That was close. I almost got caught. Oh, goodness!

21
00:03:10,720 --> 00:03:12,030
Hi, Joo Young Jae.

22
00:03:12,690 --> 00:03:15,299
- It's been a while. - Gosh, he got caught?

23
00:03:15,300 --> 00:03:17,130
- Su Bin. - He asked me to keep it a secret.

24
00:03:21,500 --> 00:03:22,570
You startled me.

25
00:03:23,440 --> 00:03:25,110
I have a thing about bouquets.

26
00:03:27,710 --> 00:03:29,940
That's why I prepared this bouquet. Go on, hit me.

27
00:03:44,690 --> 00:03:49,100
Thanks to you, Director, our show got its highest ratings ever.

28
00:03:49,860 --> 00:03:50,860
All right!

29
00:03:51,130 --> 00:03:52,930
To show our gratitude, we were hoping...

30
00:03:53,030 --> 00:03:54,740
you'd appear on our segment just one more time.

31
00:03:54,940 --> 00:03:57,640
- That's why I came all this way. - Is this how you show gratitude?

32
00:03:58,210 --> 00:04:00,570
- Please, I'm asking you. - Is that the only reason you came?

33
00:04:01,140 --> 00:04:02,640
Well, you shouldn't have turned your phone off.

34
00:04:03,610 --> 00:04:04,680
Because it was off...

35
00:04:05,610 --> 00:04:07,380
It's been a while since I've been back in my hometown too, so...

36
00:04:07,720 --> 00:04:11,020
this is really nice. It's all thanks to you, Director.

37
00:04:11,220 --> 00:04:12,220
And here I got my hopes up.

38
00:04:15,360 --> 00:04:16,860
Well, what do you know. Your phone's working fine.

39
00:04:16,960 --> 00:04:19,089
Was Jin Su's restaurant called "A Lavish Feast?"

40
00:04:19,090 --> 00:04:20,130
Where was it again?

41
00:04:20,490 --> 00:04:22,900
- Why don't you look it up with it? - Right.

42
00:04:24,600 --> 00:04:25,600
Well then, bye.

43
00:04:27,270 --> 00:04:28,270
Director.

44
00:04:28,870 --> 00:04:30,570
Director, wait a minute.

45
00:04:31,410 --> 00:04:34,170
Director, let me take you there. Just a moment.

46
00:04:34,880 --> 00:04:37,910
If you appear on the show just one more time, it'll change my life.

47
00:04:38,210 --> 00:04:39,410
Take a right at that intersection.

48
00:04:39,850 --> 00:04:43,279
First, I'll get a pay raise, and I'll have a stable income,

49
00:04:43,280 --> 00:04:44,589
so I can cut back on out-of-town gigs.

50
00:04:44,590 --> 00:04:46,250
And there are so, so many good things about that,

51
00:04:46,320 --> 00:04:47,450
but it would take too long to explain...

52
00:04:47,720 --> 00:04:49,320
Are you okay with me being on the show?

53
00:04:49,520 --> 00:04:52,630
Of course, I am. My life is about to get a whole lot better.

54
00:04:52,760 --> 00:04:54,330
What do my personal feelings matter?

55
00:04:56,630 --> 00:04:57,630
Did Producer Gyeong say that?

56
00:04:58,270 --> 00:04:59,870
That if I appear on the show, your life will get better?

57
00:05:00,200 --> 00:05:01,200
So, will you do it?

58
00:05:02,500 --> 00:05:03,570
Goodness.

59
00:05:04,440 --> 00:05:05,440
(Mom)

60
00:05:05,441 --> 00:05:07,140
Su Bin, what should I do?

61
00:05:07,670 --> 00:05:09,080
I don't think I can make it out today.

62
00:05:10,440 --> 00:05:11,450
Have you eaten?

63
00:05:13,010 --> 00:05:14,010
Do you want to get something to eat together?

64
00:05:15,320 --> 00:05:17,850
Gosh. Eat up now, okay?

65
00:05:18,250 --> 00:05:20,290
- Thanks for the food. - Thank you for the food.

66
00:05:36,940 --> 00:05:38,140
Why can't your mom make it?

67
00:05:39,410 --> 00:05:42,480
- I don't know. - You could've gone to her house.

68
00:05:44,410 --> 00:05:45,410
I don't know.

69
00:05:54,290 --> 00:05:55,290
Goodness.

70
00:05:57,460 --> 00:05:59,389
- You mean the day after tomorrow? - Thank you for the meal.

71
00:05:59,390 --> 00:06:00,889
- Thanks. - Is Jin Su doing well?

72
00:06:00,890 --> 00:06:01,899
Oh, of course.

73
00:06:01,900 --> 00:06:03,000
(A Lavish Feast)

74
00:06:03,060 --> 00:06:04,529
He's the same as always.

75
00:06:04,530 --> 00:06:07,300
Oh, please don't apologise, Chief. You don't have to.

76
00:06:07,500 --> 00:06:09,500
- Come back again soon, okay? - Sure, I will.

77
00:06:12,410 --> 00:06:15,280
Sure, even if you call me on the same day, I'll come running.

78
00:06:15,810 --> 00:06:17,580
Of course, especially since you always request me.

79
00:06:18,110 --> 00:06:21,550
Yes, sir. Yes, thank you. Yes, goodbye.

80
00:06:23,020 --> 00:06:24,620
They're booking you for a festival the day after tomorrow?

81
00:06:25,220 --> 00:06:26,790
It's obviously a last-minute replacement.

82
00:06:27,190 --> 00:06:29,320
I'm thankful for it. Fill-in gigs pay more.

83
00:06:30,290 --> 00:06:31,630
This is how hard I work.

84
00:06:32,230 --> 00:06:34,230
But if you would just agree to be on the show?

85
00:06:40,330 --> 00:06:41,870
See? It's because it's peak festival season right now.

86
00:06:42,270 --> 00:06:43,400
Oh, never mind. It's Producer Gyeong.

87
00:06:45,740 --> 00:06:48,810
- Yes, sir. - Joo Yi Jae, why haven't I heard?

88
00:06:49,510 --> 00:06:50,510
Did he say he won't do it?

89
00:06:51,850 --> 00:06:53,650
We're talking about it now.

90
00:06:53,850 --> 00:06:55,850
He seems very busy preparing for his next project.

91
00:06:55,980 --> 00:06:59,590
- We're coordinating his schedule. - What if we get fired before then?

92
00:06:59,890 --> 00:07:01,420
I told you to hurry it up.

93
00:07:01,960 --> 00:07:03,720
I told you I'm talking to him.

94
00:07:05,190 --> 00:07:07,360
Why are you so impatient?

95
00:07:10,030 --> 00:07:12,170
- Will things change if I do it? - Hey, hey!

96
00:07:12,630 --> 00:07:16,270
- What? - Will Joo Yi Jae's life change?

97
00:07:16,340 --> 00:07:18,240
Hey, you. Are you crazy?

98
00:07:18,310 --> 00:07:22,110
- What's gotten into you? - You said life would get easier.

99
00:07:23,140 --> 00:07:24,140
So that's what I'm going to do.

100
00:07:26,880 --> 00:07:28,020
I'm saying I'll do it.

101
00:07:50,770 --> 00:07:51,940
We need a new gas canister.

102
00:07:52,010 --> 00:07:53,510
Yes, a butane canister. Coming right up.

103
00:07:55,740 --> 00:07:57,740
I gave you a generous two-person serving.

104
00:07:57,840 --> 00:07:59,280
I'll get it for you. Yes. On the house, on the house.

105
00:08:02,520 --> 00:08:04,319
The sashimi is drying out. Serve it.

106
00:08:04,320 --> 00:08:06,390
Come on. Then you should hire another part-timer.

107
00:08:07,320 --> 00:08:10,120
I'm... I'm sorry. Yes, here's your sashimi rice bowl.

108
00:08:10,920 --> 00:08:12,129
- More side dishes, please. - Of course.

109
00:08:12,130 --> 00:08:14,699
- More side dishes coming up. - Sir.

110
00:08:14,700 --> 00:08:16,400
(To Simsim Seafood, Sim Yu Geon, Stay Healthy.)

111
00:08:18,470 --> 00:08:21,030
- Did you enjoy your meal? - Yes.

112
00:08:23,000 --> 00:08:24,910
Who is that? Do you know who that is?

113
00:08:25,440 --> 00:08:26,970
- I don't know. - Is he a singer?

114
00:08:27,310 --> 00:08:28,580
He's our owner's son.

115
00:08:29,380 --> 00:08:32,410
- He's handsome, right? - I thought you were the son.

116
00:08:33,180 --> 00:08:37,550
That young man and the owner...

117
00:08:38,550 --> 00:08:39,550
do look alike.

118
00:08:39,890 --> 00:08:41,290
And he's also my former classmate.

119
00:08:42,320 --> 00:08:45,190
- Are you here on vacation? - Yes.

120
00:08:46,560 --> 00:08:48,330
Is your son famous?

121
00:08:48,400 --> 00:08:51,000
Yes, my son is an actor.

122
00:08:51,500 --> 00:08:52,870
- An actor? - Really?

123
00:08:52,930 --> 00:08:53,930
What has he been in?

124
00:08:54,000 --> 00:08:56,539
He debuted as Friend Three in "Devil High."

125
00:08:56,540 --> 00:08:57,640
And in "The Young Master of My Garden,"

126
00:08:57,700 --> 00:08:59,270
he gave a passionate performance in Episode 4, Scene 27.

127
00:08:59,340 --> 00:09:00,770
And in "I Won't Love Anymore", he had the golden line...

128
00:09:01,210 --> 00:09:04,240
in the scene right before the end of Episode Eight.

129
00:09:04,680 --> 00:09:06,850
"Director, the car is waiting."

130
00:09:07,680 --> 00:09:08,920
And many others.

131
00:09:12,720 --> 00:09:14,420
- Many. - Many.

132
00:09:14,690 --> 00:09:15,720
We've been here too long. Let's go, let's go.

133
00:09:15,790 --> 00:09:17,860
- Sir, the meal was delicious. - Yes, it was very tasty.

134
00:09:17,920 --> 00:09:20,460
- Come again. Thank you. - Okay.

135
00:09:21,430 --> 00:09:23,230
They didn't watch it. Just clear it all away.

136
00:09:23,600 --> 00:09:24,600
Yes.

137
00:09:28,040 --> 00:09:29,970
(To Simsim Seafood, Sim Yu Geon, Stay Healthy.)

138
00:09:34,610 --> 00:09:36,640
It came out so pretty.

139
00:09:46,990 --> 00:09:49,390
I wonder if he's trying hard somewhere.

140
00:09:50,390 --> 00:09:53,230
(Audition: "Smile of First Love")

141
00:09:53,330 --> 00:09:55,500
- Yes, Eun Soo. - Thank goodness.

142
00:10:04,340 --> 00:10:05,470
Sim Yu Geon.

143
00:10:07,870 --> 00:10:10,240
- Yes? - You can come in.

144
00:10:22,420 --> 00:10:26,190
I'm afraid your image doesn't quite fit our character.

145
00:10:26,990 --> 00:10:27,990
Marriage?

146
00:10:30,000 --> 00:10:31,300
I thought I made myself clear.

147
00:10:32,170 --> 00:10:33,170
Then kill him.

148
00:10:33,430 --> 00:10:34,500
Okay.

149
00:10:36,640 --> 00:10:37,640
Are you...

150
00:10:39,010 --> 00:10:40,640
Are you sure that we're alive?

151
00:10:42,280 --> 00:10:43,280
Next.

152
00:10:43,780 --> 00:10:44,780
That's a shame.

153
00:11:09,000 --> 00:11:12,540
Ha Na, the revised schedule is out.

154
00:11:16,140 --> 00:11:17,580
Just a second, Director Kang.

155
00:11:19,650 --> 00:11:21,110
Why am I the only one with a day off?

156
00:11:21,680 --> 00:11:22,820
Do I have another event on my schedule...

157
00:11:22,880 --> 00:11:23,980
that I don't know about again?

158
00:11:24,850 --> 00:11:26,520
That day...

159
00:11:26,720 --> 00:11:29,890
You and CEO Ahn have a scheduled event together.

160
00:11:30,990 --> 00:11:32,230
What is it this time?

161
00:11:32,990 --> 00:11:34,690
We have to go accept an award for a major donation.

162
00:11:35,230 --> 00:11:36,230
Just a moment.

163
00:11:37,130 --> 00:11:38,130
Let's step outside.

164
00:11:38,900 --> 00:11:41,130
The image of an exemplary mother and daughter, together.

165
00:11:41,470 --> 00:11:42,570
Wouldn't that look great?

166
00:11:45,740 --> 00:11:49,040
The exemplary mother can just go receive it. Why do I have to?

167
00:11:49,310 --> 00:11:52,150
- So I can be your accessory again? - Does that upset you?

168
00:11:53,380 --> 00:11:55,679
Hey, why would that upset you? It's an honour.

169
00:11:55,680 --> 00:11:58,050
The fact that you don't understand why I'm upset...

170
00:11:58,120 --> 00:11:59,120
is what's upsetting me.

171
00:11:59,420 --> 00:12:00,620
You think I'm the only one affected by this?

172
00:12:01,090 --> 00:12:03,360
Who do you think has to suffer when filming gets delayed?

173
00:12:03,490 --> 00:12:07,830
- The other staff and actors, right? - That's a part of their job.

174
00:12:08,930 --> 00:12:12,130
Powerful people get to wield time as they please, Ha Na.

175
00:12:12,400 --> 00:12:14,600
Aren't you embarrassed to live like that, Mom?

176
00:12:14,730 --> 00:12:17,500
I'm so happy that you get to live well thanks to me.

177
00:12:18,140 --> 00:12:20,010
It makes me feel like this is why I worked so relentlessly.

178
00:12:20,240 --> 00:12:22,710
I'm miserable because people say I only get by thanks to you.

179
00:12:23,480 --> 00:12:26,280
Come on, you silly girl. You don't even know what real misery is.

180
00:12:29,320 --> 00:12:31,750
Don't you dare go around apologising on set again like last time.

181
00:12:31,990 --> 00:12:33,890
You think people will respect you for that?

182
00:12:34,090 --> 00:12:35,220
It just makes you look foolish.

183
00:12:35,320 --> 00:12:38,060
No, you're the one making me look foolish.

184
00:12:38,090 --> 00:12:40,189
It's only natural to apologise when you do something wrong.

185
00:12:40,190 --> 00:12:42,099
And besides, my mistakes are usually your fault anyway.

186
00:12:42,100 --> 00:12:44,459
Hey, keep it down. The place is crawling with rats,

187
00:12:44,460 --> 00:12:45,930
just waiting to dig something up.

188
00:12:48,740 --> 00:12:53,110
Oh my, CEO Ahn. I'm so sorry. I'm a little late, aren't I?

189
00:12:53,210 --> 00:12:54,840
Oh, I know you came in after waiting outside.

190
00:12:55,280 --> 00:12:56,309
You're so considerate.

191
00:12:56,310 --> 00:13:00,010
By the way, who did Ha Na's hair? I've never seen her before.

192
00:13:00,080 --> 00:13:02,019
Oh, Si Hyeon is her usual stylist,

193
00:13:02,020 --> 00:13:03,820
but this one is fast and has great taste, so...

194
00:13:03,880 --> 00:13:04,880
Change her.

195
00:13:05,520 --> 00:13:07,190
What is with her hair? No taste at all.

196
00:13:08,520 --> 00:13:10,860
- Now. - Oh, okay.

197
00:13:16,930 --> 00:13:19,270
Really? Su Bin came here?

198
00:13:19,400 --> 00:13:22,470
Really. I'm telling you, he was just at my restaurant for bibimbap.

199
00:13:22,540 --> 00:13:25,610
- With Yi Jae. Just only two. - Oh my gosh.

200
00:13:27,670 --> 00:13:31,280
But didn't they say his father sent him to the States to study?

201
00:13:31,540 --> 00:13:34,780
I haven't seen hide nor hair of him. I figured he'd be a doctor by now.

202
00:13:35,220 --> 00:13:37,419
Then the one on TV with Yi Jae,

203
00:13:37,420 --> 00:13:39,750
that film director, is he really Mr. Woo's son?

204
00:13:39,950 --> 00:13:42,559
That's right. He completely changed his name,

205
00:13:42,560 --> 00:13:44,090
I almost didn't recognise him.

206
00:13:44,420 --> 00:13:46,159
How did he suddenly become a Lee?

207
00:13:46,160 --> 00:13:48,829
You said his name was Lee An Woo or Lee An Gu, right?

208
00:13:48,830 --> 00:13:51,160
Yes. It's funny, isn't it?

209
00:13:51,230 --> 00:13:53,100
It was Yi Jae who was always running around,

210
00:13:53,170 --> 00:13:54,770
saying she was going to make movies.

211
00:13:54,870 --> 00:13:57,600
- How did he manage that? - I know, right?

212
00:13:57,800 --> 00:14:01,570
- Su Bin's at my house. - Oh, ma'am, you scared me.

213
00:14:01,840 --> 00:14:04,840
- What are you doing out here? - Waiting for the bus.

214
00:14:04,940 --> 00:14:06,050
I see.

215
00:14:07,610 --> 00:14:09,420
Hey, hey. Look, they are coming.

216
00:14:09,780 --> 00:14:11,420
- That's them. - Where? Who?

217
00:14:11,480 --> 00:14:13,919
- It is. - It's the two of them, right?

218
00:14:13,920 --> 00:14:14,920
Where?

219
00:14:15,360 --> 00:14:17,620
- Over there. - Hey, see? It's them, right?

220
00:14:17,790 --> 00:14:20,860
Those two are always attached at the hip, then and now.

221
00:14:21,830 --> 00:14:24,560
- So pretty. - But ma'am...

222
00:14:24,960 --> 00:14:26,830
You don't run that inn anymore, do you?

223
00:14:27,530 --> 00:14:29,470
I was wondering if something came up.

224
00:14:31,740 --> 00:14:33,970
- Oh, the bus is here. - Yes.

225
00:14:34,040 --> 00:14:36,010
- Go on, get your things done. - Okay. Okay.

226
00:14:36,080 --> 00:14:37,780
- We're off. - Okay.

227
00:14:40,810 --> 00:14:42,250
Grandma.

228
00:14:42,850 --> 00:14:44,120
Grandma.

229
00:14:45,450 --> 00:14:46,490
She's not here.

230
00:14:47,950 --> 00:14:48,960
You can give it to her.

231
00:14:49,690 --> 00:14:50,690
Okay.

232
00:14:50,990 --> 00:14:51,990
Wait a minute.

233
00:15:10,940 --> 00:15:12,109
I'm giving this back.

234
00:15:12,110 --> 00:15:13,150
(Gyeongseong Love Song)

235
00:15:16,920 --> 00:15:19,350
When you gave me this script, you said you'd wait.

236
00:15:20,150 --> 00:15:21,760
I think it belongs with you now.

237
00:15:24,620 --> 00:15:27,030
So now you're returning my dream to me?

238
00:15:29,460 --> 00:15:33,170
Are you sure about that? What if I rip it up or burn it?

239
00:15:33,830 --> 00:15:36,040
If that's the ending you want, then do it.

240
00:15:37,770 --> 00:15:40,170
I overlooked the fact that I'm just a part of your past...

241
00:15:40,410 --> 00:15:41,810
and only thought about moving forward.

242
00:15:43,010 --> 00:15:44,140
I realised I was wrong.

243
00:15:45,550 --> 00:15:48,280
Our ending should have come first, not the script's ending.

244
00:15:50,050 --> 00:15:51,520
I'm truly sorry.

245
00:15:55,120 --> 00:15:57,020
I'm sorry I didn't realise it on my own,

246
00:15:58,690 --> 00:15:59,860
and I'm sorry it took me so long.

247
00:16:02,730 --> 00:16:04,600
Those years you spent waiting...

248
00:16:06,170 --> 00:16:09,000
were years I didn't want to remember.

249
00:16:13,440 --> 00:16:14,770
All because of that?

250
00:16:15,240 --> 00:16:18,310
That's why you bombed your CSAT? A man, because of some girl?

251
00:16:18,380 --> 00:16:21,750
It's not because of her. I never wanted to go to med school.

252
00:16:21,820 --> 00:16:23,950
- Su Bin, apologise to him. Now. - You get out now.

253
00:16:24,680 --> 00:16:25,690
Mom.

254
00:16:26,050 --> 00:16:28,520
Don't, just don't.

255
00:16:32,060 --> 00:16:34,290
Hit me, until you're satisfied.

256
00:16:37,930 --> 00:16:39,030
As punishment for that,

257
00:16:40,100 --> 00:16:42,400
my father tried to send me to the US,

258
00:16:43,570 --> 00:16:46,010
and until I said I would do as he said,

259
00:16:46,640 --> 00:16:48,370
I wasn't even allowed to leave the house.

260
00:16:55,750 --> 00:16:56,880
It only took ten days,

261
00:16:58,850 --> 00:17:00,450
for me to give up on myself.

262
00:17:04,960 --> 00:17:05,960
I'll go.

263
00:17:06,930 --> 00:17:07,930
To the U.S.

264
00:17:08,660 --> 00:17:10,460
I'll live the life you want for me.

265
00:17:15,540 --> 00:17:16,540
Good.

266
00:17:18,270 --> 00:17:19,710
That's all you had to do.

267
00:17:23,380 --> 00:17:24,580
But you...

268
00:17:25,880 --> 00:17:28,110
How could you believe in me more than I believed in myself?

269
00:17:31,020 --> 00:17:32,150
That big heart of yours...

270
00:17:33,750 --> 00:17:35,290
made me feel even more ashamed.

271
00:17:39,860 --> 00:17:40,930
I'm not asking you...

272
00:17:41,790 --> 00:17:44,530
to understand or forgive me.

273
00:17:46,430 --> 00:17:47,430
I just...

274
00:17:48,230 --> 00:17:49,440
hope your heart...

275
00:17:49,800 --> 00:17:51,470
can feel a little bit better.

276
00:17:53,940 --> 00:17:54,970
Right.

277
00:17:55,740 --> 00:17:56,740
What a relief.

278
00:17:58,010 --> 00:17:59,380
It wasn't my fault after all.

279
00:18:01,180 --> 00:18:03,080
There were circumstances beyond your control.

280
00:18:05,020 --> 00:18:06,050
So that's what it was.

281
00:18:14,930 --> 00:18:16,260
But I don't feel better.

282
00:18:18,870 --> 00:18:22,000
You're saying this now and calling it a consolation?

283
00:18:24,340 --> 00:18:26,110
To the person you once loved,

284
00:18:26,770 --> 00:18:28,810
do you know the worst way to be remembered?

285
00:18:30,440 --> 00:18:33,850
It's not to be remembered as a jerk, but as a pathetic one.

286
00:18:35,750 --> 00:18:36,820
You pathetic one.

287
00:18:39,490 --> 00:18:40,490
(Gyeongseong Love Song)

288
00:19:01,770 --> 00:19:03,040
Oh, my goodness.

289
00:19:06,750 --> 00:19:07,750
You're here.

290
00:19:07,810 --> 00:19:09,819
I washed that to make barley tea,

291
00:19:09,820 --> 00:19:11,520
and you're sticking it before I could drink it.

292
00:19:11,720 --> 00:19:13,520
I'm sorry. I didn't know.

293
00:19:14,120 --> 00:19:15,519
- Have you eaten? - Not yet.

294
00:19:15,520 --> 00:19:17,660
What were you so busy with that you couldn't even eat?

295
00:19:18,460 --> 00:19:20,490
I was waiting to eat with you.

296
00:19:20,660 --> 00:19:24,260
- You sweet talker. Let's go inside. - Okay. The yard's clean, isn't it?

297
00:19:24,330 --> 00:19:25,870
It does look clean.

298
00:19:26,430 --> 00:19:27,430
Good job.

299
00:19:28,770 --> 00:19:30,600
(Closed)

300
00:19:31,240 --> 00:19:32,810
You could've at least told me you were coming.

301
00:19:33,440 --> 00:19:36,110
- I would've made you something. - I'll just have some noodles.

302
00:19:37,210 --> 00:19:38,210
Mom...

303
00:19:39,450 --> 00:19:40,980
I don't have the deposit money yet.

304
00:19:41,510 --> 00:19:43,350
Tell the landlord to wait a little longer.

305
00:19:43,450 --> 00:19:45,990
If worst comes to worst, I can just sell the shop.

306
00:19:46,690 --> 00:19:48,720
You said you'd buy the house back soon after you sold it.

307
00:19:48,920 --> 00:19:51,420
And now you're selling the shop too? I'll get the money.

308
00:19:52,130 --> 00:19:53,830
- You think you can do it? - I have to.

309
00:19:55,530 --> 00:19:56,830
When do you think you'll have it?

310
00:19:57,130 --> 00:19:59,070
I feel so sorry about keeping them waiting.

311
00:20:00,770 --> 00:20:02,270
What about me? Don't you feel sorry for me?

312
00:20:04,400 --> 00:20:06,410
If I start feeling sorry for you, there'd be no end to it.

313
00:20:06,470 --> 00:20:07,470
So I just stopped.

314
00:20:08,140 --> 00:20:10,040
I already feel bad enough that you were born my daughter.

315
00:20:11,610 --> 00:20:13,810
Pay me back. This isn't a gift.

316
00:20:14,380 --> 00:20:16,080
You know what that money means to me, don't you?

317
00:20:16,180 --> 00:20:17,450
By riding boat and going over mountains,

318
00:20:17,520 --> 00:20:20,750
- I earned it falling over paddies. - Of course, I know.

319
00:20:21,790 --> 00:20:22,790
By the way...

320
00:20:24,520 --> 00:20:25,990
I saw him on your show.

321
00:20:29,760 --> 00:20:30,830
I'm done.

322
00:20:35,100 --> 00:20:38,300
Mom, did you know I got our highest ratings ever?

323
00:20:38,370 --> 00:20:40,610
I'm the jewel of my show these days. A real jewel.

324
00:20:41,370 --> 00:20:44,940
Never mind Producer Gyeong, even the Chief Producer absolutely adores me.

325
00:20:45,010 --> 00:20:46,010
Really?

326
00:20:46,510 --> 00:20:48,049
Never mind them fawning over you.

327
00:20:48,050 --> 00:20:50,250
You should've gotten something out of it.

328
00:20:50,550 --> 00:20:54,520
Of course. Who do you think I am? I'm Joo Yi Jae, daughter of Hyun Ok.

329
00:20:54,990 --> 00:20:57,560
Good grief, girl. You're all talk.

330
00:20:57,860 --> 00:20:59,689
- It's fine. I'll do it. - Move aside.

331
00:20:59,690 --> 00:21:01,530
- I said it's fine. - Move.

332
00:21:02,630 --> 00:21:05,130
Wow, you're strong. Why are you so strong?

333
00:21:06,230 --> 00:21:08,130
- All right. - What have you been eating?

334
00:21:09,140 --> 00:21:10,940
I never skip meals, you know.

335
00:21:27,520 --> 00:21:29,190
Don't you dare tell Mom about this.

336
00:21:32,490 --> 00:21:33,490
An additional fee for my silence.

337
00:21:37,360 --> 00:21:38,900
You've got some nerve for someone who just got caught.

338
00:21:39,230 --> 00:21:40,230
Bye.

339
00:21:54,410 --> 00:21:56,880
(2011 Bunam Youth Film Festival, Grand Prize: Joo Yi Jae)

340
00:22:00,490 --> 00:22:02,490
(Gyeongseong Love Song)

341
00:22:13,700 --> 00:22:15,230
This raw fish soup is on the house.

342
00:22:16,540 --> 00:22:19,140
Wow, Su Bin, you've gotten even more handsome.

343
00:22:20,070 --> 00:22:22,509
It's so good to see him after so long. It makes me so happy.

344
00:22:22,510 --> 00:22:25,110
Right? I'm so happy too.

345
00:22:25,910 --> 00:22:27,510
- Thank you so much. - Of course.

346
00:22:27,810 --> 00:22:30,380
- Thank you. - Don't thank me. It's nothing.

347
00:22:31,450 --> 00:22:32,490
Enjoy your meal.

348
00:22:33,450 --> 00:22:34,450
Eat up, son.

349
00:22:34,720 --> 00:22:35,720
You too, Mom.

350
00:22:36,220 --> 00:22:38,360
You like your wraps with white kimchi.

351
00:22:41,190 --> 00:22:42,260
Here, have some.

352
00:22:46,270 --> 00:22:47,270
Is it good?

353
00:22:47,530 --> 00:22:49,200
It tastes even better coming from my son.

354
00:22:50,440 --> 00:22:52,510
You know, it's been a while since I've had raw fish.

355
00:22:52,570 --> 00:22:54,240
It's because you've been eating much nicer food, right?

356
00:22:54,370 --> 00:22:58,180
Eating with you is the best meal in the world for me.

357
00:22:59,280 --> 00:23:00,280
I'm sorry...

358
00:23:00,610 --> 00:23:03,850
- for not calling more often. - We can see each other like this.

359
00:23:04,750 --> 00:23:07,190
I'm just so excited that you're back in Korea.

360
00:23:08,320 --> 00:23:09,360
So...

361
00:23:10,160 --> 00:23:11,820
Today it's my treat.

362
00:23:12,260 --> 00:23:15,230
Here, try it. Oh my, you might spill.

363
00:23:20,470 --> 00:23:21,500
Su Bin...

364
00:23:23,070 --> 00:23:24,570
Is it still hard for you to come visit?

365
00:23:26,470 --> 00:23:27,470
Next time.

366
00:23:28,540 --> 00:23:29,910
Your father...

367
00:23:31,540 --> 00:23:33,450
He's not like that because he hates you.

368
00:23:34,050 --> 00:23:35,050
Mom.

369
00:23:39,690 --> 00:23:41,250
Okay. I'm sorry, son.

370
00:23:42,720 --> 00:23:44,260
Please, stop apologising.

371
00:23:45,630 --> 00:23:46,660
Come on, get in.

372
00:23:50,660 --> 00:23:52,330
Call me next time you're in town, okay?

373
00:23:52,770 --> 00:23:54,000
I'll be waiting.

374
00:23:54,430 --> 00:23:55,430
Okay.

375
00:24:07,110 --> 00:24:08,180
Go on, Mom.

376
00:25:05,870 --> 00:25:09,080
(No Jaywalking)

377
00:25:12,280 --> 00:25:14,150
- I'm sorry. - I'm sorry.

378
00:25:30,800 --> 00:25:34,070
- I'm not going to the audition. - You promised. We'd make a movie.

379
00:25:34,130 --> 00:25:35,200
Like that even matters.

380
00:25:37,500 --> 00:25:40,540
- Stop calling my name. - You promised.

381
00:25:54,850 --> 00:25:56,120
What do you think you're doing!

382
00:26:54,510 --> 00:26:55,550
Are you okay?

383
00:26:58,680 --> 00:26:59,950
I'm just a little dizzy.

384
00:27:16,900 --> 00:27:17,900
Su Bin.

385
00:27:18,940 --> 00:27:20,470
I eat carrots now.

386
00:27:22,310 --> 00:27:23,740
I figured if I'm going to do this for a living,

387
00:27:24,480 --> 00:27:26,750
I can't be a picky eater.

388
00:27:28,850 --> 00:27:30,920
That's how much time has passed.

389
00:27:31,620 --> 00:27:32,990
Enough for us to have changed.

390
00:27:37,990 --> 00:27:39,190
But why...

391
00:27:41,560 --> 00:27:44,000
Why are there some things that never seem to get better?

392
00:27:47,000 --> 00:27:49,440
The good memories start to fade,

393
00:27:51,500 --> 00:27:53,070
but why do the bad ones...

394
00:27:54,510 --> 00:27:55,840
still feel so vivid?

395
00:27:59,550 --> 00:28:01,080
Maybe that's why, with good memories,

396
00:28:02,620 --> 00:28:04,320
you have to hold on to them even tighter, don't you think?

397
00:28:11,220 --> 00:28:12,560
That's why I came back.

398
00:28:29,180 --> 00:28:31,710
Yes, PD Gyeong. I just need to go to Jeonju Station, correct?

399
00:28:31,810 --> 00:28:32,810
Yes.

400
00:28:35,750 --> 00:28:36,920
Watch out.

401
00:28:45,690 --> 00:28:46,690
Oh, my.

402
00:28:50,760 --> 00:28:51,760
(Black Raspberry Wine)

403
00:28:53,530 --> 00:28:54,530
(Arrowroot Juice)

404
00:28:54,530 --> 00:28:55,530
(Jangsu Honey)

405
00:29:05,310 --> 00:29:06,610
(Gyeongseong Love Song)

406
00:29:15,220 --> 00:29:18,660
(Gyeongseong Love Song)

407
00:29:22,230 --> 00:29:23,660
The title is "Gyeongseong Love Song".

408
00:29:24,030 --> 00:29:26,200
It's about a gisaeng named Nan Yeong who dreams of being a poet.

409
00:29:26,370 --> 00:29:30,300
But after her dearest friend is shot and killed,

410
00:29:30,370 --> 00:29:32,339
she lives only for revenge.

411
00:29:32,340 --> 00:29:34,470
(Written And Directed By Joo Yi Jae, Woo Su Bin)

412
00:29:41,880 --> 00:29:45,990
Then, a man appears before her as if by fate.

413
00:29:46,490 --> 00:29:48,950
Mu Gyeom, a son of a rich family.

414
00:29:49,050 --> 00:29:51,620
Of course, you've got to have a rich kid.

415
00:29:51,890 --> 00:29:54,330
Poetry, wine, and women.

416
00:29:54,660 --> 00:29:58,130
A man who enjoys life's pleasures with not a care in the world.

417
00:29:58,330 --> 00:30:01,570
How could any woman not fall in love with a man like that?

418
00:30:02,600 --> 00:30:04,270
But he...

419
00:30:04,700 --> 00:30:07,610
was an independence fighter in the guise of a playboy.

420
00:30:08,110 --> 00:30:11,180
But don't be shocked yet. The real twist is...

421
00:30:11,410 --> 00:30:14,950
he's the enemy she's spent her whole life looking for.

422
00:30:15,280 --> 00:30:18,480
Revenge or love? That is the question.

423
00:30:19,020 --> 00:30:20,020
Bang.

424
00:30:28,060 --> 00:30:30,360
So someone dies in the end?

425
00:30:32,300 --> 00:30:34,700
Someone has to. It's a melodrama. It's supposed to be sad.

426
00:30:38,040 --> 00:30:39,740
But I like happy endings.

427
00:30:40,710 --> 00:30:42,740
(Gyeongseong Love Song)

428
00:31:14,870 --> 00:31:16,180
- Hey. - Yes?

429
00:31:16,840 --> 00:31:18,980
Do you remember when I came to you saying I wanted to make movies?

430
00:31:21,550 --> 00:31:25,050
How could I forget? You had no money and no luggage.

431
00:31:25,120 --> 00:31:27,690
You just showed up with nothing but that one screenplay.

432
00:31:27,750 --> 00:31:28,750
Exactly.

433
00:31:29,520 --> 00:31:31,589
Even when it was hard and I wanted to quit,

434
00:31:31,590 --> 00:31:32,990
I held onto it and persevered.

435
00:31:34,030 --> 00:31:37,400
That was why Yi Jae gave it to me. So I wouldn't give up.

436
00:31:38,200 --> 00:31:39,670
She wanted us to share the same dream.

437
00:31:40,830 --> 00:31:42,030
That's why she held on to me.

438
00:31:43,770 --> 00:31:44,869
I realised it too late.

439
00:31:44,870 --> 00:31:47,810
And that's why you worked like a madman.

440
00:31:47,970 --> 00:31:49,170
Maybe that's why I lost her?

441
00:31:50,540 --> 00:31:52,950
I came this far thanks to that screenplay.

442
00:31:54,850 --> 00:31:58,920
What if Yi Jae gave up on everything because I had the screenplay?

443
00:32:03,190 --> 00:32:04,690
I have no idea what you're talking about.

444
00:32:05,120 --> 00:32:06,230
Just eat.

445
00:32:08,030 --> 00:32:09,900
The screenplay of "The Gyeongseong Love Song..."

446
00:32:11,000 --> 00:32:12,100
I gave it back to her.

447
00:32:12,500 --> 00:32:14,200
- But I haven't heard back yet. - What?

448
00:32:16,100 --> 00:32:17,200
Keep it down.

449
00:32:17,600 --> 00:32:19,040
Hey. You...

450
00:32:19,200 --> 00:32:22,170
No way. It means a lot to us.

451
00:32:22,740 --> 00:32:23,879
She can't just throw that away.

452
00:32:23,880 --> 00:32:26,480
But either way, you don't have it now, do you?

453
00:32:26,650 --> 00:32:29,480
- No, I don't. - Right. Nope. I'm heading back.

454
00:32:29,550 --> 00:32:31,949
I still haven't found soft tofu stew better than in LA,

455
00:32:31,950 --> 00:32:33,620
and I'm not crazy about you either.

456
00:32:33,720 --> 00:32:38,420
My dream of moving out is over. I'm leaving. I'm out of here.

457
00:32:38,920 --> 00:32:40,630
You scanned it, right?

458
00:32:42,560 --> 00:32:43,560
I did?

459
00:32:44,330 --> 00:32:47,200
- No, I didn't. - Oh, come on.

460
00:32:48,300 --> 00:32:50,300
You're taking this joke too far.

461
00:32:52,840 --> 00:32:53,840
You're kidding, right?

462
00:32:56,280 --> 00:32:58,240
A little closer, closer.

463
00:32:58,780 --> 00:33:00,210
All right. See you later.

464
00:33:09,790 --> 00:33:10,890
Congratulations on your marriage.

465
00:33:12,190 --> 00:33:13,530
Thank you.

466
00:33:14,360 --> 00:33:15,560
It's beautiful.

467
00:33:18,060 --> 00:33:19,230
We have our orders from headquarters.

468
00:33:20,130 --> 00:33:21,170
We're moving to Plan B.

469
00:33:30,180 --> 00:33:32,440
Cut. Okay.

470
00:33:32,740 --> 00:33:35,309
- Let's get ready for lunch. - How was it?

471
00:33:35,310 --> 00:33:38,720
- Good work, everyone. - Director, how was that?

472
00:33:40,550 --> 00:33:44,490
- Five rolls of gimbap. - Yes. Wait, what? Five rolls?

473
00:33:44,620 --> 00:33:45,660
That Ko Sang Yeon...

474
00:33:45,820 --> 00:33:48,790
I saved some for you. You should eat in your van.

475
00:33:48,860 --> 00:33:50,929
The CEO told me to make sure you eat in the van...

476
00:33:50,930 --> 00:33:52,300
I'm going to eat outside.

477
00:33:52,700 --> 00:33:54,199
But your dress is uncomfortable.

478
00:33:54,200 --> 00:33:55,570
Why don't you just eat inside with me?

479
00:33:55,730 --> 00:33:57,240
I can do a backflip in this thing.

480
00:33:57,740 --> 00:33:59,509
And don't worry about me. You go eat now.

481
00:33:59,510 --> 00:34:00,940
Before Ko Sang Yeon eats it all.

482
00:34:01,740 --> 00:34:03,510
But your dress...

483
00:34:27,100 --> 00:34:28,200
What about it?

484
00:34:31,040 --> 00:34:32,070
Nothing.

485
00:34:43,520 --> 00:34:45,180
I really hate filming right now.

486
00:34:48,390 --> 00:34:49,390
Excuse me?

487
00:34:52,620 --> 00:34:54,230
Am I not allowed to hate filming?

488
00:34:55,530 --> 00:34:57,760
No, of course, you can feel that way.

489
00:35:02,530 --> 00:35:03,900
You didn't get any?

490
00:35:04,700 --> 00:35:06,840
No. They said they ran out.

491
00:35:08,310 --> 00:35:09,710
That jerk Ko Sang Yeon...

492
00:35:13,310 --> 00:35:14,910
- Want some? - I'm okay.

493
00:35:15,010 --> 00:35:17,320
I can't finish a whole roll anyway. Have some.

494
00:35:18,620 --> 00:35:20,520
My arm is getting tired.

495
00:35:22,450 --> 00:35:23,460
Well then.

496
00:35:24,820 --> 00:35:25,920
Thank you.

497
00:35:47,280 --> 00:35:50,150
You're bored, aren't you? Henchman 3.

498
00:35:51,480 --> 00:35:53,850
- I should get going now. - What?

499
00:35:55,320 --> 00:35:58,160
You're done right after lunch? That's a sweet gig.

500
00:35:58,320 --> 00:36:00,560
The only reason I can't leave is because of you, Ha Na.

501
00:36:02,790 --> 00:36:04,100
You're saying my name like a prayer.

502
00:36:05,300 --> 00:36:06,870
I'm a Buddhist, by the way.

503
00:36:07,470 --> 00:36:09,530
Just call me Ha Na.

504
00:36:10,700 --> 00:36:11,700
Okay.

505
00:36:13,340 --> 00:36:15,670
By the way, the thing you're sitting on...

506
00:36:16,540 --> 00:36:17,880
is my motorcycle.

507
00:36:23,880 --> 00:36:25,380
- Get on. - What?

508
00:36:25,420 --> 00:36:27,050
Can't you give me a ride? Just once.

509
00:36:28,750 --> 00:36:31,090
Come on, I even gave you some of my gimbap. Just for ten minutes.

510
00:36:32,620 --> 00:36:33,660
Five minutes?

511
00:36:34,460 --> 00:36:35,460
Fine.

512
00:36:35,860 --> 00:36:38,160
- We'll call it even for the gimbap. - Awesome.

513
00:36:44,040 --> 00:36:45,040
Like this?

514
00:37:06,320 --> 00:37:08,190
This feels like a scene from a movie.

515
00:37:08,790 --> 00:37:10,760
Huh? What movie?

516
00:37:11,500 --> 00:37:12,960
That Hong Kong movie...

517
00:37:14,830 --> 00:37:16,300
Never mind.

518
00:37:28,550 --> 00:37:29,780
What was that?

519
00:37:30,580 --> 00:37:33,250
I almost died. Did you see that?

520
00:37:34,190 --> 00:37:38,390
- We'd both be dead. Hold on tight. - Okay.

521
00:37:57,680 --> 00:37:59,010
I feel so alive.

522
00:37:59,710 --> 00:38:01,080
Thanks, Yu Geon.

523
00:38:03,380 --> 00:38:04,580
Chae Yeon.

524
00:38:04,650 --> 00:38:08,720
Oh, hey. Where have you been? I've been looking everywhere for you.

525
00:38:09,090 --> 00:38:10,390
She remembered.

526
00:38:12,960 --> 00:38:16,290
- Gosh, what's that on your head? - A helmet.

527
00:38:16,900 --> 00:38:18,660
Wait... A helmet?

528
00:38:22,600 --> 00:38:25,300
(Topline Entertainment)

529
00:38:33,810 --> 00:38:38,620
Ma'am. Ma'am. Producer Jaden has arrived.

530
00:38:39,080 --> 00:38:40,089
What?

531
00:38:40,090 --> 00:38:42,120
Producer Jaden has arrived in Korea.

532
00:38:42,690 --> 00:38:45,420
Should I book a sushi restaurant in Cheongdam for the meeting?

533
00:38:46,430 --> 00:38:49,129
- Why? - You said it was the best sushi.

534
00:38:49,130 --> 00:38:52,029
And I'm supposed to recommend the best sushi of my life...

535
00:38:52,030 --> 00:38:53,330
to a Korean-American?

536
00:38:54,070 --> 00:38:57,200
He likes Korean food. Find a genuine Korean restaurant.

537
00:38:57,600 --> 00:38:59,239
One that serves beautiful side dishes.

538
00:38:59,240 --> 00:39:01,109
Yes, ma'am. And the meeting with Writer Noh Su Rin...

539
00:39:01,110 --> 00:39:03,810
Hey, hey. Stop. Just send me a text.

540
00:39:05,480 --> 00:39:07,610
Unbelievable. Who called this a stairway to paradise?

541
00:39:08,080 --> 00:39:09,750
I feel like I'm at the gates of agony.

542
00:39:12,550 --> 00:39:15,350
Speaking of which, where did Ha Na go?

543
00:39:16,020 --> 00:39:17,120
Well...

544
00:39:18,160 --> 00:39:19,690
She said she was looking for someone.

545
00:39:23,300 --> 00:39:25,160
- And? - Yes, I helped her find them.

546
00:39:25,660 --> 00:39:27,200
So, who was it?

547
00:39:27,670 --> 00:39:29,670
- Well... - Goodness.

548
00:39:33,040 --> 00:39:34,740
Are you playing 20 Questions with me?

549
00:40:00,770 --> 00:40:02,070
Who's there?

550
00:40:10,680 --> 00:40:11,880
I came to return this.

551
00:40:14,210 --> 00:40:16,380
Smells delicious.

552
00:40:17,580 --> 00:40:20,690
I work part-time at a barbecue restaurant.

553
00:40:22,550 --> 00:40:23,560
Here.

554
00:40:24,860 --> 00:40:26,490
The sunset was really pretty.

555
00:40:30,700 --> 00:40:32,700
How long have you been waiting?

556
00:40:32,760 --> 00:40:33,799
By the way...

557
00:40:33,800 --> 00:40:35,900
You must be seeing me every day. How are you not a fan yet?

558
00:40:47,050 --> 00:40:50,050
But how did you know where I live?

559
00:40:55,020 --> 00:40:56,050
This.

560
00:41:00,490 --> 00:41:02,760
(Sim Yu Geon)

561
00:41:04,300 --> 00:41:07,770
- But my address isn't on here. - I can't stop thinking about it.

562
00:41:07,930 --> 00:41:11,540
- Excuse me? About what? - Riding on your motorcycle.

563
00:41:13,570 --> 00:41:15,610
I've never felt anything like that before.

564
00:41:20,710 --> 00:41:22,510
Could you give me another ride sometime?

565
00:41:24,850 --> 00:41:25,850
Okay.

566
00:41:27,150 --> 00:41:30,590
But why are you being like this toward me?

567
00:41:31,290 --> 00:41:32,290
Why?

568
00:41:32,560 --> 00:41:33,830
Because...

569
00:41:35,190 --> 00:41:36,390
you're scaring me.

570
00:41:38,460 --> 00:41:40,569
- Am I scary? - No, I mean...

571
00:41:40,570 --> 00:41:42,670
But this always works in the dramas.

572
00:41:43,700 --> 00:41:46,500
- It works? What does? - Maybe it only works in dramas.

573
00:41:47,370 --> 00:41:50,540
You should know, I'm actually good at everything else.

574
00:41:50,610 --> 00:41:52,339
I'm good at somersaults, shooting,

575
00:41:52,340 --> 00:41:55,080
horseback riding, and even jumping from high places.

576
00:41:55,150 --> 00:41:57,080
- I see. - But...

577
00:41:59,280 --> 00:42:01,120
I don't know how to make friends.

578
00:42:02,850 --> 00:42:04,420
That's why I don't have any.

579
00:42:12,530 --> 00:42:13,600
Do you...

580
00:42:14,870 --> 00:42:16,430
want to be a friend?

581
00:42:20,940 --> 00:42:21,940
Well...

582
00:42:27,480 --> 00:42:28,480
Yes.

583
00:42:29,010 --> 00:42:31,020
Then let's be friends.

584
00:42:32,280 --> 00:42:33,280
Friends.

585
00:42:36,220 --> 00:42:37,220
Really?

586
00:42:37,820 --> 00:42:38,820
Yes.

587
00:42:42,490 --> 00:42:45,260
Then let's call this a gift to celebrate our friendship.

588
00:42:49,200 --> 00:42:50,340
I...

589
00:42:51,040 --> 00:42:52,870
I'll get going now, friend.

590
00:42:53,770 --> 00:42:56,840
Bye. Friend.

591
00:43:00,910 --> 00:43:03,350
She seems to know how to make friends just fine.

592
00:43:26,470 --> 00:43:28,870
- It's been a while, Jaden. - Hello, CEO Ahn.

593
00:43:29,240 --> 00:43:32,980
No, wait, should I call you CEO Seo now?

594
00:43:34,280 --> 00:43:35,280
Whatever you're comfortable with.

595
00:43:35,550 --> 00:43:38,050
I never thought I'd see you smiling in front of me, CEO Seo.

596
00:43:38,420 --> 00:43:40,790
Perhaps it came sooner than you thought?

597
00:43:42,120 --> 00:43:43,890
You've gotten thick-skinned,

598
00:43:44,960 --> 00:43:46,890
and it's nice to see you've become a little jaded.

599
00:43:48,630 --> 00:43:49,630
Let's order first.

600
00:43:50,930 --> 00:43:53,670
Talking business on an empty stomach makes me sick.

601
00:44:04,640 --> 00:44:05,680
Let me pour it.

602
00:44:09,080 --> 00:44:12,980
So, CEO Seo, you're willing to co-produce?

603
00:44:14,120 --> 00:44:15,720
Since I'm starting in a foreign land,

604
00:44:16,090 --> 00:44:18,390
I was hoping to be led by someone I can trust and follow.

605
00:44:18,620 --> 00:44:21,760
And you think I'm that person?

606
00:44:21,890 --> 00:44:23,500
You were the one who reached out to me, weren't you?

607
00:44:24,930 --> 00:44:25,930
How naive.

608
00:44:26,760 --> 00:44:28,330
You have no idea what I'll demand.

609
00:44:29,700 --> 00:44:32,570
Let's talk about the project once the first draft is out.

610
00:44:35,310 --> 00:44:37,910
I'm more interested in what's behind it.

611
00:44:39,440 --> 00:44:40,980
How much are you willing to tell me?

612
00:44:41,280 --> 00:44:43,880
Of course, I'll tell you everything I know.

613
00:44:45,850 --> 00:44:47,989
I heard there's quite a story behind that script.

614
00:44:47,990 --> 00:44:50,790
Something about a first love was going around?

615
00:44:51,620 --> 00:44:54,630
However, that only applies if you're my partner.

616
00:44:55,860 --> 00:44:56,960
And you're not my partner yet.

617
00:44:57,860 --> 00:45:00,030
So, I have to be a little careful.

618
00:45:14,180 --> 00:45:16,580
In that case, I'll contact you once the first draft is ready.

619
00:45:17,420 --> 00:45:18,550
- All right. - Okay, ma'am.

620
00:45:39,240 --> 00:45:40,510
- Director Kang. - Yes?

621
00:45:41,510 --> 00:45:44,510
What does it mean if he came all this way but won't come in?

622
00:45:45,010 --> 00:45:46,140
Maybe he feels uncomfortable?

623
00:45:49,450 --> 00:45:51,150
Uncomfortable? About what?

624
00:45:52,080 --> 00:45:53,080
I'm sorry.

625
00:45:59,720 --> 00:46:01,160
You don't have to walk on eggshells around me.

626
00:46:01,630 --> 00:46:03,260
You said CEO Ahn was our best option anyway, right?

627
00:46:03,660 --> 00:46:05,130
Yes, as of now, she is.

628
00:46:06,330 --> 00:46:09,170
And I'm not being sensitive. I'm just really mad right now.

629
00:46:12,170 --> 00:46:14,140
You need to go get that script from Yi Jae.

630
00:46:14,810 --> 00:46:16,370
- Why? - What do you mean, why?

631
00:46:16,440 --> 00:46:18,009
You went on and on about that script on air,

632
00:46:18,010 --> 00:46:20,110
and it doesn't even have a first draft.

633
00:46:20,710 --> 00:46:22,809
Hey, everyone I meet asks about it.

634
00:46:22,810 --> 00:46:24,780
CEO Ahn even brought up some story about a first love.

635
00:46:26,520 --> 00:46:27,520
No way.

636
00:46:28,750 --> 00:46:29,750
Dude.

637
00:46:29,920 --> 00:46:33,360
Yes, right. Yes, I said it was me. I said I was the first love.

638
00:46:38,300 --> 00:46:39,300
(Yi Jae)

639
00:46:39,300 --> 00:46:40,300
Gosh.

640
00:46:43,000 --> 00:46:44,400
Hello?

641
00:46:44,900 --> 00:46:46,840
Where are you? Get to Sangam right now.

642
00:46:47,110 --> 00:46:49,740
PD Gyeong wants to have a meeting. I'm texting you the address.

643
00:46:52,540 --> 00:46:54,579
Why are you going to the meeting? You?

644
00:46:54,580 --> 00:46:56,310
I don't get why you're the one going to the meeting.

645
00:46:56,980 --> 00:46:57,980
Go.

646
00:46:58,720 --> 00:47:00,720
Go and find out if the script is dead or alive.

647
00:47:01,090 --> 00:47:02,550
- Yes, sir. - Good.

648
00:47:03,690 --> 00:47:04,690
Please, get off.

649
00:47:21,210 --> 00:47:22,270
My phone.

650
00:47:37,620 --> 00:47:40,020
Hey, hey, it's still early. What gives?

651
00:47:40,220 --> 00:47:42,389
- Stop drinking. The taxi's here. - Really?

652
00:47:42,390 --> 00:47:43,660
- Come on, come on. - Who called this?

653
00:47:43,730 --> 00:47:46,160
- I did. - No. Let's have one more.

654
00:47:46,360 --> 00:47:48,800
Yes, come on, back to your wife.

655
00:47:48,930 --> 00:47:50,840
She's the reason I don't want to go home.

656
00:47:50,900 --> 00:47:54,770
- But you love your wife. - Hey, I don't love her. I don't.

657
00:47:54,840 --> 00:47:58,910
- Sir, take care of him. In you go. - Seriously.

658
00:47:59,940 --> 00:48:02,410
I'm not going. I'm really not going. I'm not!

659
00:48:06,350 --> 00:48:09,690
- What's going on? We had a meeting. - You're here?

660
00:48:10,520 --> 00:48:12,960
- Is everyone gone? - It's over.

661
00:48:13,390 --> 00:48:15,290
Why are you so late?

662
00:48:15,390 --> 00:48:17,600
Already? I even printed out the questions.

663
00:48:18,200 --> 00:48:19,200
I called him too.

664
00:48:19,260 --> 00:48:22,030
Who? You brought a puppy? Where is it?

665
00:48:22,270 --> 00:48:24,699
Woo Su Bin. Director Ian.

666
00:48:24,700 --> 00:48:26,940
Oh, right, him. Okay.

667
00:48:27,470 --> 00:48:31,910
He's appearing on the show anyway, right? Then it's fine.

668
00:48:32,180 --> 00:48:34,950
I'll take care of everything,

669
00:48:35,580 --> 00:48:36,580
so, you can just stay out of it.

670
00:48:36,650 --> 00:48:38,819
Since when have you ever taken care of anything?

671
00:48:38,820 --> 00:48:40,850
Did you even have a meeting today? Tell me.

672
00:48:41,390 --> 00:48:44,159
You didn't call me to be your designated driver, right?

673
00:48:44,160 --> 00:48:45,220
What? Designated driver?

674
00:48:47,360 --> 00:48:48,590
Bingo.

675
00:48:50,430 --> 00:48:52,860
You know, when you're the one driving,

676
00:48:53,030 --> 00:48:55,500
it's more comfortable than my own mattress.

677
00:48:56,100 --> 00:48:57,540
I'm counting on you.

678
00:49:02,070 --> 00:49:03,340
Joo Yi Jae can't drive.

679
00:49:03,740 --> 00:49:05,340
- What? - She's been drinking.

680
00:49:07,880 --> 00:49:10,180
You were drinking, Ms. Joo Yi Jae. With me.

681
00:49:13,580 --> 00:49:16,450
Oh, I'm dizzy. How did I even get here?

682
00:49:16,550 --> 00:49:17,890
Why am I here?

683
00:49:18,360 --> 00:49:20,060
How did I get here? Oh, I'm so dizzy.

684
00:49:20,190 --> 00:49:22,790
You were perfectly fine until now. What are you talking about?

685
00:49:22,860 --> 00:49:26,630
- This is why day drinking is hard. - You smell like alcohol, though.

686
00:49:33,970 --> 00:49:34,970
Is he always like this?

687
00:49:35,110 --> 00:49:38,580
Well, he drinks and makes me work,

688
00:49:38,640 --> 00:49:41,680
he drinks and dumps his work on me, and makes me be his DD...

689
00:49:41,750 --> 00:49:43,310
Hey, Joo Yi Jae.

690
00:49:44,050 --> 00:49:45,950
But he's not a bad person.

691
00:49:46,050 --> 00:49:48,590
We've been close since college, so, for about ten years now?

692
00:49:48,650 --> 00:49:51,490
- That's right. - No, he is a bad person.

693
00:49:51,690 --> 00:49:55,930
Hey. What do you think you're doing? I'm right here.

694
00:49:55,990 --> 00:49:58,000
Then what do you think you're doing to Yi Jae?

695
00:49:58,060 --> 00:50:00,970
What? What are you talking about?

696
00:50:02,670 --> 00:50:03,770
I know everything.

697
00:50:04,670 --> 00:50:07,070
Should I say it? Or will you?

698
00:50:07,540 --> 00:50:09,539
"Yi Jae Will Be There" is going to be cancelled...

699
00:50:09,540 --> 00:50:10,540
in the upcoming reshuffle.

700
00:50:11,080 --> 00:50:12,880
You punk, couldn't you try to do a better job?

701
00:50:12,980 --> 00:50:16,380
All I hear is how the PD is riding on his reporter's coattails.

702
00:50:16,980 --> 00:50:18,519
Just keep the ratings up.

703
00:50:18,520 --> 00:50:19,880
Hitting a new peak would be even better.

704
00:50:20,280 --> 00:50:23,990
You do that, and I'll take care of you no matter what.

705
00:50:25,260 --> 00:50:26,690
I'll do my best.

706
00:50:33,300 --> 00:50:34,300
That's enough.

707
00:50:35,430 --> 00:50:36,530
I'll hear it from him myself.

708
00:50:37,400 --> 00:50:38,670
Get in.

709
00:50:39,070 --> 00:50:41,140
- Get what? - I said get in.

710
00:50:41,740 --> 00:50:42,910
Oh, okay.

711
00:50:56,450 --> 00:50:58,920
- You said you were drinking. - I didn't.

712
00:50:59,460 --> 00:51:01,190
Just answer me straight.

713
00:51:01,260 --> 00:51:03,390
Hey, this is my mom's car. She's still paying for it.

714
00:51:04,260 --> 00:51:06,100
- Am I getting fired? - Hey, I think I'm going to be sick.

715
00:51:10,640 --> 00:51:11,640
Hey, watch it.

716
00:51:16,840 --> 00:51:18,280
And you used me?

717
00:51:20,340 --> 00:51:21,350
Hey.

718
00:51:22,350 --> 00:51:23,350
Hey, Joo Yi Jae.

719
00:51:24,150 --> 00:51:25,420
Hey, I'm sorry.

720
00:51:26,180 --> 00:51:28,890
The living has to go on living.

721
00:51:29,850 --> 00:51:32,090
No, that's not what I meant.

722
00:51:32,590 --> 00:51:34,490
Hey, watch out! Look out. No.

723
00:51:38,260 --> 00:51:39,700
Hey, look out, look out!

724
00:51:58,450 --> 00:52:02,090
I wonder, when exactly did I become dead to you?

725
00:52:02,450 --> 00:52:05,420
My career has always been disposable, I know.

726
00:52:06,360 --> 00:52:09,460
- But this is just wrong. - No, Yi Jae... Listen.

727
00:52:10,060 --> 00:52:12,900
Listen to me. Hey, where are you going?

728
00:52:14,430 --> 00:52:15,870
Why? Oh, no.

729
00:52:17,000 --> 00:52:19,070
We're over. As of today.

730
00:52:19,540 --> 00:52:20,609
- Get out. - What?

731
00:52:20,610 --> 00:52:22,839
- I said, get out. - Hey, hey, wait. No, it's just...

732
00:52:22,840 --> 00:52:24,840
- Get out. - Let's just talk.

733
00:52:25,010 --> 00:52:26,010
Get out.

734
00:52:29,050 --> 00:52:30,050
What?

735
00:52:30,580 --> 00:52:32,320
- Hey. I'll stitch it up. - Come here.

736
00:52:32,680 --> 00:52:34,790
Come here. Get out. Get out!

737
00:52:38,160 --> 00:52:39,160
Yi Jae.

738
00:52:40,320 --> 00:52:41,330
Hey.

739
00:52:42,030 --> 00:52:45,300
Hey, the car key. Hey, what are you doing? Hey!

740
00:52:48,500 --> 00:52:49,500
What?

741
00:52:50,800 --> 00:52:52,270
That crazy...

742
00:52:53,300 --> 00:52:54,440
Oh, for goodness' sake.

743
00:52:56,010 --> 00:52:57,680
Hey, my key.

744
00:53:02,310 --> 00:53:03,310
Where...

745
00:53:04,180 --> 00:53:06,220
Hey. Joo Yi Jae.

746
00:53:54,930 --> 00:53:56,100
I feel like...

747
00:53:56,900 --> 00:53:59,070
I've been living my life in such a rush.

748
00:54:00,140 --> 00:54:02,210
Just putting out one fire after another.

749
00:54:04,310 --> 00:54:06,480
That job I took because I needed the money...

750
00:54:07,140 --> 00:54:11,620
Who knew it'd turn into a week, then a month, and then years?

751
00:54:12,520 --> 00:54:14,350
That in itself is amazing.

752
00:54:16,850 --> 00:54:20,190
- That's why you're in high demand. - But...

753
00:54:20,620 --> 00:54:22,130
it's not like I'm the only one.

754
00:54:24,360 --> 00:54:27,030
If Yi Jae doesn't show up for "Yi Jae Will Be There," who will?

755
00:54:28,400 --> 00:54:29,400
That's true.

756
00:54:31,340 --> 00:54:33,200
I guess I chose the wrong title.

757
00:54:33,500 --> 00:54:34,910
"Yi Jae Will Be There."

758
00:54:35,770 --> 00:54:36,970
And that's why I'm leaving.

759
00:54:40,310 --> 00:54:41,810
I didn't love it,

760
00:54:42,480 --> 00:54:43,750
but it was important to me.

761
00:54:46,250 --> 00:54:47,590
It fed me...

762
00:54:48,420 --> 00:54:49,820
and paid off my debts.

763
00:55:04,370 --> 00:55:05,370
You jerk.

764
00:55:08,010 --> 00:55:09,440
Why do you keep following me around,

765
00:55:09,870 --> 00:55:11,210
not even letting me cry?

766
00:55:38,200 --> 00:55:39,200
Yi Jae.

767
00:55:48,710 --> 00:55:50,850
So, this is what you meant when you said being pathetic is the worst.

768
00:55:53,920 --> 00:55:55,320
Because you can never forget it.

769
00:56:01,290 --> 00:56:02,360
Right now,

770
00:56:04,760 --> 00:56:05,830
you seem a little pathetic.

771
00:56:07,360 --> 00:56:08,370
You are.

772
00:56:13,440 --> 00:56:15,310
Even though I knew I could never forget you anyway.

773
00:56:29,920 --> 00:56:30,920
Su Bin...

774
00:56:33,490 --> 00:56:35,030
You're not what I regret.

775
00:56:38,060 --> 00:56:39,060
It's me.

776
00:58:19,000 --> 00:58:20,000
Gosh.

777
00:58:21,630 --> 00:58:22,630
Ian.

778
00:58:29,640 --> 00:58:31,780
- Let's go get some breakfast. - In Wook.

779
00:58:35,650 --> 00:58:36,880
Hey, hold on.

780
00:58:38,350 --> 00:58:39,350
It's cold.

781
00:59:38,210 --> 00:59:40,310
(Dream To You)

782
00:59:40,710 --> 00:59:41,850
I look forward to working with you.

783
00:59:42,180 --> 00:59:44,980
Please stay at the hotel until your studio is set up.

784
00:59:45,350 --> 00:59:46,450
You have to write the screenplay.

785
00:59:46,920 --> 00:59:48,320
You were laughing at me earlier, weren't you?

786
00:59:48,690 --> 00:59:51,560
Who do you think you are, messing with my friend? Come on, let's go.

787
00:59:52,020 --> 00:59:55,160
If you're stuck in the same house together all day,

788
00:59:55,290 --> 00:59:57,390
your eyes will wander, and so will your heart.

789
00:59:57,730 --> 01:00:00,560
And it'll turn into a steamy R-rated romance.

790
01:00:01,270 --> 01:00:02,330
What's there to think about?

791
01:00:03,400 --> 01:00:04,400
Don't you think...

792
01:00:05,100 --> 01:00:06,100
we're about to do it?